  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Chase's spell changed the game, says Gambhir after India's defeat vs WI",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/chase-s-spell-changed-the-game-says-gambhir-after-india-s-defeat-vs-wi-126101000005_1.html",
      "description": "India head coach Gautam Gambhir on Friday credited Roston Chase's disciplined spell in the middle overs for checking India's charge, but said the hosts needed to find ways to defend big totals after West Indies pulled off a record chase to win the second T20I by six wickets here.\nChase returned figures of 3/24, dismissing Abhishek Sharma, Ishan Kishan and Shivam Dube in the middle overs to slow India down after a flying start.\n\"If you look at the context of the game, it was a game-changing, match-winning spell. The way he changed his lines was important on this wicket. But against dangerous teams like West Indies, we need to find a way to defend totals,\" Gambhir said in the post-match press conference.\n\"You have to keep changing your lines and make the batters guess. If you keep bowling the same line and length, they can settle in. He bowled at the batters' legs, went wide and bowled full. He kept changing his approach, and those variations are very important on wickets like these,\"",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T06:34:15"
    },
    {
      "title": "IND vs WI: West Indies stun India with second-highest chase in T20I history",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/cricket/news/ind-vs-wi-west-indies-stun-india-with-second-highest-chase-in-t20i-history-126101000212_1.html",
      "description": "West Indies' record chase against India in the second T20I was also their highest successful run chase in T20I history, surpassing their 232-run chase against South Africa back in 2025",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-10T04:52:27"
    }
  ]
